# Safety copies of the object database taken before a history rewrite. Each one
# is a full .git clone sitting inside the work tree: git would record it as a
# nested-repository entry, which is useless in a public history and would drag
# unreachable objects along with it.
.git.backup_*/
.git.backup_*.tar
.git.backup_*.zip

# Private research artifacts (source, notes, parameter configs) are excluded
# locally via .git/info/exclude, which is never committed. Keeping the concrete
# names there means this public file stays free of project-specific identifiers.